          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em Kan-fibrant simplicial manifold
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+manifold"} simplicial manifold
            (for instance
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+manifold"} topological manifold
            or simplicial
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            = succeed "-condition" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horns"} horns
            have continuous/smooth fillers in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+neighbourhoods"} open neighbourhoods
            of all points, but possibly not globally.)
          %p
            Motivated by the standard way (see at
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+hypothesis"} homotopy hypothesis
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complexes"} Kan complexes
            (hence Kan-fibrant
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometrically+discrete+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} geometrically discrete ∞-groupoids
            and given that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoid
            is an example of a locally Kan-fibrant simplicial manifold (a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-truncated"} 1-truncated
            one), such Kan-fibrant simplicial manifolds are often referred to
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+infinity-groupoids"} Lie infinity-groupoids
            (or
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+n-groupoids"} Lie n-groupoids
            for finite
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-truncated+object+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} truncation
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Zhu06"} Zhu 06
          %p
            With such a suitably local definition, there should be the structure of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopical+category"} homotopical category
            on Kan-fibrant simplicial manifolds which embeds homotopically full and faithful into a local
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            over a suitable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            of manifolds, hence such that this inclusion presents and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} full sub-(∞,1)-category
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaf+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-sheaf (∞,1)-topos
            over manifolds (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"}> smooth ∞-groupoids
            ”).
          %p
            Some care is needed in correctly interpreting the “Lie” condition in view of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            %em every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stack"} ∞-stack
            on the category of smooth manifolds (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"}> smooth ∞-groupoid
            ”) is presented by a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+manifold"} simplicial manifold
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#NSS12"} NSS 12, section 2.2
          %p
            A homotopy-correct characterization of the sub-
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            \-category presented by the Kan-fibrant simplicial objects as that of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+%E2%88%9E-stacks"} geometric ∞-stacks
            modeled on manifolds is in (
            %a{:href => "#Pridham09"}> Pridham 09
            ) (see around p. 17 for the differential geometric version).
          %p
            Kan-fibrant simplicial manifolds have received particular attention as the result of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integration
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebroids"} L-∞ algebroids
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integration
            for more on that.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                Any ordinary
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial object
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
                of a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoid
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
                of any
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundles"} principal bundles
                with this
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
                as a structure group.
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold%E2%80%93Kan+functor"} Dold–Kan functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
                applied to any nonnegatively graded
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
                of abelian Lie groups.
            %li
              %p
                In particular, applying
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
                to the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{U}(1)[n]
                = succeed "-gerbes." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
            %li
              %p
                The nonabelian analogue of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
                applied to any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+module"} crossed module
                whose two constituent groups are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groups"} Lie groups
                and the involved homomorphisms and actions are smooth.
            %li
              %p
                The nonabelian analogue of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
                applied to any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercrossed+complex"} hypercrossed complex
                whose constituent groupoids are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoids"} Lie groupoids
                and the involved homomorphisms and actions are smooth.
            %li
              %p
                As a special case of the previous example, any
                %span.newWikiWord
                  simplicial Lie group
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/simplicial+Lie+group"} ?
                is a Kan simplicial manifold.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+manifold"} simplicial manifold
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+differential+geometry"} higher differential geometry
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} internal ∞-groupoid
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} smooth ∞-groupoid
          %h2#references References
          %p Early appearances of the concept include
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Henriques"}> André Henriques
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Integrating
                    = succeed "-algebras" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi L
                              %mn ∞
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0603563"} arXiv:math/0603563
            %li#Zhu06
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chenchang+Zhu"}> Chenchang Zhu
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                    \-groupoids and stacky Lie groupoids
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0609420"} arXiv:math/0609420
            %li#Zhu08
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chenchang+Zhu"}> Chenchang Zhu
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Kan replacement of simplicial manifolds
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0812.4150"} arXiv:0812.4150
          %p
            Characterization of the homotopy theory of Kan-fibrant simplicial manifolds as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+%E2%88%9E-stacks"} geometric ∞-stacks
            modeled on smooth manifolds is in (see aroung p. 17 for the differential geometric version)
          %ul
            %li#Pridham09
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Pridham"}> Jonathan Pridham
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Presenting higher stacks as simplicial schemes
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0905.4044"} arXiv:0905.4044
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-bundles"} principal ∞-bundles
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi SmoothMfd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} = Sh_\infty(SmoothMfd)
            which are represented by locally Kan-fibrant simplicial manifolds is in
          %ul
            %li#NSS12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Nikolaus"}> Thomas Nikolaus
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Danny+Stevenson"} Danny Stevenson
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Principal+%E2%88%9E-bundles+--+theory%2C+presentations+and+applications"} Principal ∞-bundles – Presentations
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1207.0249"} arXiv:1207.0249
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jesse+Wolfson"}> Jesse Wolfson
                ,
                %em
                  Descent for
                  = succeed "-Bundles" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1308.1113"}> arXiv:1308.1113
                )
